1
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Ted is coming.

2
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Ted is a comedy, fantasy film directed by Seth MacFarlane.

3
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:09,000
John Bennett, a man whose childhood wish of bringing his teddy bear to life came true, now must
decide between keeping the relationship with the bear or his girlfriend, Lori.

4
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:30,000
John Bennett, played by Mark Wahlberg.

5
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Lori Collins, played by Mila Kunis.

6
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Ted (voice), played by Seth MacFarlane.

7
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:33,000
Rex, played by Joel McHale.

8
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Donny, played by Giovanni Ribisi.

9
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:15,000
Guy, played by Patrick Warburton.

10
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
Ted (stylized in all lowercase) is a 2012 American  fantasy buddy stoner comedy film directed and co-produced by Seth
MacFarlane and written by MacFarlane, Alec Sulkin, and Wellesley Wild based on a story written by MacFarlane.

11
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:57,000
The first installment in the Ted franchise, the film stars Mark Wahlberg and Mila Kunis, with Joel McHale and Giovanni
Ribisi in supporting roles, and MacFarlane providing the voice and motion capture of the title character.

12
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
The story follows John Bennett, a Boston native whose childhood
wish brings his teddy bear friend Ted to life.

13
01:09:33,000 --> 01:09:39,000
However, in adulthood, Ted and John's friendship begins to interfere with the progression
of John's worklife and his relationship with his girlfriend, Lori Collins.

14
01:14:54,000 --> 01:15:00,000
MacFarlane's feature-length directorial debut, the film was produced by Media Rights Capital, Fuzzy Door
Productions, Bluegrass Films and Smart Entertainment, and distributed by Universal Pictures.

15
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
It was released in theaters in the United States on June 29, 2012, and was a box
office hit, grossing $549.4 million against a $50–65 million budget.

16
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
Ted was the highest-grossing comedy film of the year and was
nominated for the Academy Award for Best Original Song.

17
01:30:57,000 --> 01:31:03,000
It received generally positive reviews and successfully launched a franchise, with
a sequel released in 2015 and a prequel television series in 2024.

18
01:36:18,000 --> 01:36:24,000
The film explores themes of friendship, dreams, love, buddy, teddy bear.

19
01:41:39,000 --> 01:41:45,000
The tone is lighthearted.
